---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: IT Training
description: "Structured programs in web development, QA, cloud, and data — built for graduates who want training that leads somewhere specific: a job."
glass: true
extraScripts:
  - /assets/js/count-up.js
  - /assets/js/faq-accordion.js
---
{% from "partials/icons.njk" import icon %}

{#
  This page assumes the four tracks in _data/programs.json are real, with real curricula
  and instructors. If they are not, it ships the waitlist version instead — no durations,
  no prices, no curriculum until they exist. See PRD.md §7.

  Never "guaranteed placement" anywhere on this page. Always "direct" or "priority
  access" to the placement pipeline.

  ================================================================
  Hallmark audit pass, matching job-placement.njk: hero drops the aurora/dot
  background; section heads are single-column with the label directly above the
  heading (no chapter-marker ghost index, no eyebrow on non-ordinal sections);
  the certificate grid is a definition list with inline icons on hairline rules.
  The track panels stay full-width panels — a learner comparing programs needs
  curriculum, format and prerequisites side by side. The one accent-coloured
  button (PRD §7) stays.
  ================================================================
#}

{% set crumbs = [{ label: "Home", url: "/" }, { label: "Services", url: "/services/" }, { label: "IT Training" }] %}

{# ---------- Hero ---------- #}
<section class="relative overflow-hidden">
  <div class="section-container pb-14 pt-8 sm:pb-20 sm:pt-12">
    {% include "partials/breadcrumb.njk" %}

    <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-7">
        <p class="eyebrow">Four tracks, one placement pipeline</p>

        <h1 class="mt-4 font-grotesk text-4xl font-bold leading-[1.05] tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-6xl">
          Train. Certify. Get placed.
        </h1>
        <p class="lead-copy mt-5 max-w-xl">
          Structured programs that build real skills — and feed straight into our
          placement pipeline when you're done.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row">
          {# The one accent-coloured button on the site — this audience is earlier
             in the funnel and more exploratory than the other three, per PRD §7. #}
          <a href="{{ '/contact/?role=training' | url }}"
             class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-accent px-6 py-3.5
                    font-semibold text-paper shadow-card duration-200 ease-out
                    transition-[transform,background-color] hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:bg-accent-deep">
            {{ icon("arrow-right", "w-4 h-4") }} Book a free demo class
          </a>
          <a href="{{ '/services/job-placement/' | url }}" class="btn-outline">
            See job placement
          </a>
        </div>

        {# TODO: confirm these figures with the client before launch — see stats.json. #}
        <dl class="mt-10 grid max-w-lg grid-cols-3 gap-4 border-t border-ink/10 pt-6">
          {% for stat in stats.list.slice(0, 3) %}
          <div>
            <dd class="stat-figure text-xl sm:text-2xl"
                data-count-up data-target="{{ stat.value }}" data-suffix="{{ stat.suffix }}">0{{ stat.suffix }}</dd>
            <dt class="stat-label">{{ stat.label }}</dt>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </dl>
      </div>

      <div class="relative lg:col-span-5">
        {% set coverImage = images.services["it-training"].cover %}
        <div class="glass-panel p-3">
          <img src="{{ coverImage.url }}"
               alt="{{ coverImage.alt }}"
               width="1400" height="933" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"
               class="aspect-[4/5] w-full rounded-[1.1rem] object-cover">
        </div>

        {# Frost, not pane — it floats over the photograph. See THEME.md §3. #}
        <div class="glass-frost absolute -bottom-4 left-6 rounded-2xl px-5 py-3.5 sm:-left-6">
          <p class="meta">Placement pipeline</p>
          <p class="font-grotesk text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">Direct access</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- Programs offered ----------
   Duration, format and prerequisites are the three things a learner filters on
   first, so they're on the panel, not in the FAQ. Each track stays a full panel
   rather than a grid tile. ---------- #}
<section id="programs" class="section-container scroll-mt-28 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="section-title">Tracks offered.</h2>
    <p class="lead-copy mt-4">Four programs, each ending at the same place — a portfolio project and a handoff to placement.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 space-y-5">
    {% for program in programs.list %}
    {% set shot = images.services["it-training"].tracks[program.title] %}
    {# !pt-0 because glass-panel's top padding would otherwise print a strip of
       surface above the image; the text cell carries its own padding instead. #}
    <article class="glass-panel overflow-hidden !pt-0 md:grid md:grid-cols-12">
      {% if shot %}
      <img src="{{ shot.url }}" alt="{{ shot.alt }}" width="{{ shot.width }}" height="{{ shot.height }}"
           loading="lazy"
           class="h-44 w-full object-cover md:col-span-4 md:h-full {% if loop.index is even %}md:order-last{% endif %}">
      {% endif %}
      <div class="p-5 sm:p-6 {% if shot %}md:col-span-8{% else %}md:col-span-12{% endif %}">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
          <span class="text-brand">{{ icon(program.icon, "w-5 h-5") }}</span>
          <span class="meta">{{ program.duration }}</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="mt-4 font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">{{ program.title }}</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 body-copy">{{ program.description }}</p>
        <dl class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 border-t border-dashed border-border pt-4">
          <div class="flex flex-col-reverse">
            <dt class="mt-1 meta">Format</dt>
            <dd class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">{{ program.format }}</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-col-reverse">
            <dt class="mt-1 meta">Prerequisites</dt>
            <dd class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">{{ program.prerequisites }}</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- Why train with us ----------
   The placement-pipeline link, as a pull quote — always "priority access", never
   "guaranteed placement". ---------- #}
<section id="why" class="scroll-mt-28 border-y border-white/60 bg-paper/50 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="section-container">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="assertion sm:text-3xl">
        Graduates get <span class="text-brand">direct access to our placement pipeline</span> — the file is already open on the day you certify.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink/75">
        That's priority access, not a guarantee. It's the difference between an
        open application and a recruiter who already knows your work.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- What certification means ----------
   Vague certification claims are the most common complaint about training
   providers. ---------- #}
<section id="credential" class="section-container scroll-mt-28 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="section-title">What you get at the end.</h2>
  </div>

  {% set outcomes = [
    { icon: "check-badge", t: "A completion certificate", d: "Issued by " + site.companyName + ", naming the track and the hours behind it." },
    { icon: "code", t: "A portfolio project", d: "Something you can show an employer, not a printable PDF." },
    { icon: "briefcase", t: "A handoff to placement", d: "A direct introduction into our Job Placement pipeline." }
  ] %}
  <dl class="mt-10 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-7 sm:grid-cols-3">
    {% for item in outcomes %}
    <div class="flex gap-4 border-t border-ink/15 pt-5">
      <span class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-brand">{{ icon(item.icon, "w-5 h-5") }}</span>
      <div>
        <dt class="card-title">{{ item.t }}</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1.5 body-copy">{{ item.d }}</dd>
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </dl>
  <p class="mt-8 file-inset meta max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
    Where a track prepares you for a vendor exam, we say which one and whether the exam fee is included — ask us for the track you're considering.
  </p>
</section>

{# ---------- Pricing ----------
   A page with no price signal loses price-sensitive readers entirely, so at
   minimum state that plans exist and how to get exact figures. ---------- #}
<section id="pricing" class="scroll-mt-28 border-y border-white/60 bg-paper/50 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="section-container">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="section-title">What it costs.</h2>
      <p class="lead-copy mt-4">
        Fees vary by track and format — ask for your track and we'll send exact figures. However you pay, it works one of these ways:
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-10">
      {% set paymentOptions = [
        { t: "Pay in full", d: "One payment at enrollment." },
        { t: "Installment plan", d: "A deposit at enrollment, the balance split across the program." },
        { t: "Employer reimbursement", d: "We provide the documentation your employer's tuition-assistance program needs." },
        { t: "Placement-linked deferral", d: "On select tracks — reduced cost at enrollment, the balance due after you're placed." }
      ] %}
      {% for option in paymentOptions %}
      <div class="docket-row">
        <p class="col-span-12 font-display font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:col-span-4">{{ option.t }}</p>
        <p class="col-span-12 body-copy sm:col-span-8">{{ option.d }}</p>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <a href="{{ '/contact/?role=training' | url }}" class="mt-6 link-arrow">
      Tell us your track and we'll send exact pricing {{ icon("arrow-right", "w-4 h-4") }}
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- Curriculum ----------
   The clearest literal run of the pipeline: it ends at the same Job Placement
   file. ---------- #}
<section id="procedure" class="section-container scroll-mt-28 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <p class="eyebrow">Step by step</p>
    <h2 class="section-title mt-2">From enrollment to placement.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10">
    {% set steps = [
      { label: "Enroll", description: "Pick a track and a format — online, in-person, or both." },
      { label: "Learn", description: "Structured curriculum built around real job requirements." },
      { label: "Practice", description: "A portfolio-ready project you can show employers." },
      { label: "Certification", description: "A credential that signals real, tested skill." },
      { label: "Placement support", description: "Direct handoff into our Job Placement pipeline." }
    ] %}
    {% include "partials/process-timeline.njk" %}
  </div>
</section>

{% set faqKey = "it-training" %}
{% set faqTitle = "Before you enroll." %}
{% include "partials/faq-accordion.njk" %}

{% set ctaStamp = "Ready when you are" %}
{% set ctaHeadline = "Ready to build a new skill set?" %}
{% set ctaSubtext = "Sit in on a demo class first — there's no cost and no commitment." %}
{% set ctaLabel = "Enroll Now" %}
{% set ctaHref = "/contact/?role=training" %}
{% include "partials/cta-section.njk" %}
